"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both MU and AMD disclose risks related to the procurement of critical manufacturing inputs, specifically advanced equipment and materials, and the adverse impact of supply constraints on business results. MU emphasizes the dependency on obtaining 'advanced semiconductor manufacturing equipment' to enable 'transition to lower cost manufacturing processes,' warning that inability to obtain it on a timely basis could have a 'material adverse effect' (mu_2024_1A_P050_S004, mu_2024_1A_P050_S006). Similarly, AMD states that its operations depend on 'obtaining deliveries of adequate supplies of equipment and materials of acceptable quality on a timely basis' from suppliers, and that an inability to procure a stable supply could lead to shortages or increased costs, having a 'material adverse effect on our business' (amd_2024_1A_P045_S001, amd_2024_1A_P045_S007). While MU focuses on the strategic transition to next-gen processes via equipment, AMD highlights the operational dependency on third-party service providers and the risk of sole-source limitations for specific components like memory and PCBs.",
