"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both MU and INTC disclose risks regarding environmental factors and power availability affecting operations. MU warns that 'power shortages, capacity constraints, prolonged outages' could have a material adverse effect (mu_2024_1A_P049_S002). INTC similarly identifies 'interruptions of service from utilities' and specifically highlights that 'global climate change... could disrupt the availability of water necessary for the operation of our fabrication facilities' (intc_2024_1A_P094_S001, intc_2024_1A_P094_S004). While MU broadly cites power shortages, INTC provides specific detail on water scarcity in fabrication regions like Arizona and Israel as a critical operational risk exacerbated by climate change.",
