"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both MU and NVDA disclose risks related to environmental regulations and climate change impacting supply and costs. MU notes that 'laws and regulations enacted in response to concerns regarding climate change... responsible sourcing practices' could limit material supply or increase costs (mu_2024_1A_P048_S001). NVDA similarly warns that 'climate change... its potential to increase political instability' and 'new or proposed regulations relating to carbon taxes... supply chain governance' could result in higher direct costs, including 'procurement of raw materials' and increased capital expenditures (nvda_2024_1A_P048_S004, nvda_2024_1A_P049_S002). Both companies link environmental and regulatory pressures directly to increased operational costs and supply chain limitations.",
